Z||000011||DRH||11-05-2001||09:55 AM||||Gerald,<P>Not sure how things work there, but here they give you a chance to plea bargain with the prosecuter if you say you're pleading not guilty. Racing can include a broad range of how serious the offense really was. It sounds like you were on the lower end of presenting a danger to the general public. This (along with a GENUINE apology) would tend to make a lot of judges/prosecuters be more lenient and perhaps help you keep your license. Oh, your chances depend somewhat on what your OTHER points are for too... It's worth a try anyway.<P>Good Luck.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||LoW_KeY||11-05-2001||02:15 PM||||Ohh yeah this sux.. my friend was racing a 200-2001 eclipse the car was in front and my friend decided to pass.. about 2 minutes later we see lights about a mile back  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> the cop comes up and says "what the hell were you doin" the cop swears we were goin faster then 85 in a 45 area.  The road was full of nothing just a bunch of empty land to build.  My friends car started bitching out around 80 because he stuck 86 octane in there by mistake.<P>Anyways the eclipse didn't get caught and my friend got a ticket for goin 30 over  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> sure it may seem fun but when you see lights it sucks.. and it sucks bad.<P>KC||||reg||13
Z||000013||DR650SE||11-05-2001||02:31 PM||||Yea tickets suck sooo bad.  I had 5 and my insurance was too high.  I dropped the insurance and rode a bike around till one ticket would drop of my record.  (tickets drop after 3 years in Ohio)  I just got it back and was going through a 25 at about 30-35 and my car has a LOUD exhaust.  I made a u-turn cuz I couldn't find the house I was looking for.  A man step out in the middle of the road holding up his badge in his wallet.  Then when I stoped, the cop went on about "what the phuck do you think your doing going 60 in a 25?  This little piece of schit is a death trap.  He just hated the car.  I hate him but at least he didn't give me a ticket or even a warning.  He was off duty and out side his house.  Just venting.<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||13
Z||000014||Neal||11-05-2001||02:48 PM||||Gerald stunting is worth 3 points and 116 out of your pocket.<P>Basically a cop will always be nice, when giving a ticket, unless you give him reason no to be.<BR>If you ask they have to tell you everything aswell so ask the right questions and you should get the right answer.  If you call him and meet with him just be real nice and polite, if he likes you court will go MUCH better.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Fierochic88||11-05-2001||03:53 PM||||Yesterday FieroGT914 and I were on our way to the MAFOA meeting and we were going about 75 in a 55 near my house and the cop was on the other side of the barrier.  He looked right at us and then pulled out so it kinda seemed like he was coming to turn around so we just got off at the next exit and went a different way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'll never know if he was coming for me.<P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.personal.psu.edu/users/j/j/jjr161/Fierochic88Signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||fldevel||11-05-2001||04:06 PM||||im not sure .but here in florida they cannot give you a ticket unless they can "prove" you where going that fast .. in other words if you have a radar detector and it does not go off and you get pulled over you have the right to ask him to see how fast you where going on the radar .. and if he cant prove it it is your word agenst his and u will most likely just get off with a warning ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Neal||11-05-2001||04:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierochic88:<BR><B>He looked right at us and then pulled out so it kinda seemed like he was coming to turn around so we just got off at the next exit and went a different way   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'll never know if he was coming for me.<P>Jennifer<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmm in the summer a freind of mine was on his crotch rocket doing about 200kmp/h down the highway saw a cop staring and started to see the U-turn when he passed him, he layed on the gas and saw the cop dissapear...||||reg||1
Z||000018||Brian87egotrip||11-05-2001||06:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fldevel:<BR><B>im not sure .but here in florida they cannot give you a ticket unless they can "prove" you where going that fast .. in other words if you have a radar detector and it does not go off and you get pulled over you have the right to ask him to see how fast you where going on the radar .. and if he cant prove it it is your word agenst his and u will most likely just get off with a warning </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cops cannot legally lock in the speed on a radar gun here in Fl. A buddy of mine was pulled over and didn't believe he was going as fast as the cop said. He asked to see the speed on the gun. The cop said they couldn't legally lock it in. At least that is what he told us. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000019||NorthernFiero||11-05-2001||08:07 PM|||| I got pulled over my first night of driving I wanted to beat the red light so I nailed it to the floor <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"> hit 60 to 70 mph in a 30 and the light turned red I go through and see the lights start flashing. roll down the window and there stands my old DARE officer he still knew my name <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> he said he didn't want to give me a ticket so he gave me a warning <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I'm not doing that again.<P>mike||||reg||1
